    "q-127056": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127056",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=15xy\\,i+5{x}^{2}\\,j$ and the circle $C$ given by ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=25.$ If the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: The outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C$ is $n=\\frac{x}{5}\\,i+\\frac{y}{5}\\,j.$*",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14224093/assets/d3d68329d81150c4a975bae4963d4e480cefaef0f2a0a29a0648c3793e9fb462.png)\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}(15xy\\,i+5{x}^{2}\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{x}{5}\\,i+\\frac{y}{5}\\,j)\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}3{x}^{2}y+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}4{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expression is $4{x}^{2}y.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
